## Proposal

`title`, `narrative` (MarkdownField) and `deal` (linksTo Deal). Kept deliberately separate from Quote: a Proposal sells the WHY, a Quote states the HOW MUCH. Conflating them forces every early-stage one-pager into a pricing document before the deal is qualified for one.

```ts
import { Proposal } from '@cardstack/catalog/cards/commerce/proposal';

@field proposal = linksTo(Proposal);
```

### Non-goals
Carries no pricing; that is Quote, which links back to the Proposal it formalizes. No approval or e-signature tracking.

### Example
`Proposal/acme-enterprise-renewal-proposal`, written for the `Deal/acme-enterprise-renewal` deal.
